---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const SITE = 'https://precisionsolutionstech.com';
const title = 'Passport Photo Coach Privacy Policy | Precision Solutions Tech';
const description =
  'How Passport Photo Coach for iPhone handles your photos. Everything is processed on your device; nothing is uploaded or collected.';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/` },
      {
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: 3,
        name: 'Passport Photo Coach',
        item: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/passport-photo-coach-ios/`,
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Passport Photo Coach Privacy Policy',
    url: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/passport-photo-coach-ios/`,
    description,
    dateModified: '2026-10-15',
    isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'Precision Solutions Tech', url: `${SITE}/` },
  },
];
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/legal/privacy/passport-photo-coach-ios/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li>Passport Photo Coach</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Passport Photo Coach Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: October 15, 2026</p>
      <p class="lead">
        This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Passport Photo Coach</strong> (“we”, “us”) handles
        information when you use the Passport Photo Coach app for iPhone (the “App”), published by
        <strong>Precision Solutions Tech</strong>, operated by <strong>SG TECHNOLOGY LLC</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="summary">Short version</h2>
      <p>
        Passport Photo Coach works <strong>entirely on your device</strong>. Your camera, your photos
        and everything the App measures about them stay on your iPhone. We collect no data, operate no
        account system, and run no servers that receive anything from the App. The App makes no network
        requests of its own.
      </p>

      <h2 id="camera">Camera</h2>
      <p>
        When you take a photo, the App uses the camera to coach you: it measures your face position,
        head tilt, lighting, background and accessories (such as glasses or a hat) in the live picture,
        on your device. Live frames are analysed and discarded; they are not stored or sent anywhere.
        Only the photo you take is kept, and only while you use it in the App.
      </p>

      <h2 id="photos">Photos you choose</h2>
      <p>
        If you tap “Use a photo I already have”, iOS lets you pick a photo; the App receives only the
        photo you pick and cannot see the rest of your library. If you save a photo or print sheet, the
        App asks for permission to <em>add</em> items to your Photos library. It does not read your
        library.
      </p>

      <h2 id="processing">What the App processes on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Face position and landmarks, head pose, eye and mouth openness, and lighting, to coach and crop</li>
        <li>A person outline, to measure the top of your head and, if you choose, whiten the background</li>
        <li>Whether glasses or a hat appear in the photo, using Apple’s on-device image recognition</li>
        <li>Your settings: the document you chose and whether the photo is for a baby</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        None of this is used to identify you, and none of it leaves your device. Spoken prompts use
        Apple’s on-device speech.
      </p>

      <h2 id="children">Photos of children</h2>
      <p>
        You can use the App to take ID photos of babies and children. Those photos are handled exactly
        like any other: processed on your device and never uploaded or collected by us. The App is not
        directed to children and asks no one for personal information.
      </p>

      <h2 id="sharing">Sharing and printing</h2>
      <p>
        When you share a photo (AirDrop, Messages, Mail, Files) or print it, iOS sends it where you
        choose. When you open a store’s photo website from the App, Safari opens that website, and the
        store’s own privacy policy applies to anything you upload there.
      </p>

      <h2 id="purchases">Tips</h2>
      <p>
        Optional tips in the App are processed by Apple through the App Store; we do not receive your
        payment details or Apple Account information. On the US App Store the App also links to our Buy
        Me a Coffee page, which opens in Safari; Buy Me a Coffee’s privacy policy applies there.
      </p>

      <h2 id="analytics">Analytics, tracking, and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The App contains <strong>no analytics SDKs, no advertising SDKs, and no third-party
        trackers</strong>. We do not profile you, and we do not sell or share personal information. If
        that ever changes, this policy will be updated before the change ships.
      </p>

      <h2 id="retention">Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We hold no data from the App. Photos you save to Photos or Files are yours to keep or delete.
        If you contact support, we keep your message as long as needed to help you.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy. The “Last updated” date will change when we do.</p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions:
        <a href="mailto:support@precisionsolutionstech.com">support@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/ios-apps/passport-photo-coach/">Passport Photo Coach</a>
        ·
        <a href="/ios-apps/passport-photo-coach/support/">Support</a>
        ·
        <a href="/legal/privacy/">Company privacy policy</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
